Package: comdynamite
Title: Process-Based Metacommunity Simulations with Phylogenetic Structure
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Diogo B.", "Provete", email = "dbprovete@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Simulates metacommunity dynamics with the process-based model of
    Thompson et al. (2020) <doi:10.1111/ele.13568>: density-independent growth
    that depends on the match between each species' environmental optimum and
    the local environment, Beverton-Holt competition, Poisson demographic
    stochasticity, and emigration and immigration among sites. Landscapes can
    be spatially implicit, with uniform dispersal, or explicit grids with an
    exponential dispersal kernel and a spatially autocorrelated environment,
    and the environment can change over time. Species traits (environmental
    optima, niche breadths and maximum growth rates) can carry phylogenetic
    signal or evolve under an Ornstein-Uhlenbeck process with one or several
    optima, and interspecific competition can be structured by relatedness.
    Rule-based assembly without population dynamics (limiting similarity,
    habitat filtering and neutral assembly) follows Kraft et al. (2007)
    <doi:10.1086/519400>, and static metacommunities with unimodal species
    responses follow Peres-Neto et al. (2012) <doi:10.1890/11-0494.1>. The model
    was implemented from the published equations.
